EXT. DOCKS - NIGHT

The docks are shrouded in mist, the sound of waves lapping against the piers filling the air. Vincent moves cautiously, keeping to the shadows. He spots a group of men unloading crates from a ship, their voices low and urgent.

Vincent crouches behind a stack of shipping containers, listening intently. He recognizes one of the men from the description Paulie gave him at Satriale’s. The man is clearly in charge, barking orders in Albanian.

Vincent pulls out a small camera and begins snapping photos, careful to stay hidden. He overhears snippets of conversation about a shipment of weapons and a planned move against Tony’s territory.

Suddenly, one of the men turns in Vincent’s direction, his eyes narrowing. Vincent freezes, holding his breath. After a tense moment, the man looks away, and Vincent slips back into the shadows.

Vincent feels a surge of adrenaline as he makes his way back to his car, the photos and intel safely in hand. He knows this information could be crucial in protecting Tony’s interests.
===GAME END===

